  "summary": "Puthod's division, detached to Macdonald's right before the Katzbach, was cut off by his defeat there. Marching west in the rain, it found the Bober in flood and its bridges gone at Hirschberg and again at Löwenberg. Langeron's Russians caught it at Plagwitz, east of the river; it stood on the heights with the Bober at its back until the Russian cavalry broke it. Puthod surrendered with his eagles and some 3,000 men; the rest were cut down or drowned trying to swim the river, and of a division of 7,500 almost nothing got away.",
