      "id": "plagwitz-puthod",
      "nationId": "france",
      "name": "Puthod's Division",
      "formation": "17th Division, V Corps (Lauriston)",
      "side": "French",
      "summary": "Sent off to Macdonald's right before the Katzbach, it was cut off by the defeat there and marched west to the Bober, only to find the bridges down and the river in flood. Langeron's Russians caught it at Plagwitz, east of Löwenberg, with the river at its back; it formed on the heights, was broken by the Russian cavalry, and surrendered, Puthod and his eagles with it, many men drowning as they tried to swim the Bober.",
      "notes": [
        "Built from A Clash of Eagles' French 1812 list, the nearest to 1813: there is no list for the army Napoleon raised after Russia, largely of conscripts and of battalions drawn from depots all over the Empire.",
        "After Nafziger's return of the Grande Armée for 15 August, a fortnight before; Nafziger has no order of battle for Plagwitz.",
        "Its battalions were mostly young conscripts of the classes of 1813 and 1814. They are rated as ordinary Line, as they fought: the list's Wavering or Morale 5 would suit those who broke more readily.",
        "The Irish Legion (3rd Foreign Regiment), two weak battalions of about 230 men each, is shown as Line.",
        "Regimental guns were lost in Russia and not replaced, so the division has none.",
        "The division's two foot batteries, where the list allows one, show as a historical departure.",
        "Commanders are at Staff Rating 8, the default for historical forces."
      ],
